    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Regarding those \"dead zones,\" can you touch on the secondary risks? I'm interested in how small, intermittent failures—like minor leaks from a single valve or a slightly faulty seal—might behave in that environment. How do those small, seemingly minor issues contribute to the overall escalation of a fire risk in such a dense setup?",
