      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a dense storage environment, small, intermittent leaks act as a persistent fuel source within the dead zones, slowly accumulating flammable vapor over time. These minor releases bypass the safety margin built into standard ventilation and monitoring, allowing concentrations to build to explosive levels gradually. A single small leak can become the trigger, as it provides the necessary continuous fuel for an ignition source to reach flashpoint. Ultimately, these seemingly minor defects convert a passive storage risk into an active, high-potential emergency.",
